    "answer": "I don't know. I couldn't find a date for when Otto's conversations started surviving an api restart. The sources I found show the feature exists but not when it shipped. Conversations are persisted to MongoDB (issue #23, 'A conversation survives the customer closing the tab'). The conversation-data spec also covers in-memory session cache expiry (#194) and a retention sweep (#297). Memory notes from September 2026 say #23 was not yet on main at that point, because there was no mongodb dependency, no conversations collection and no eraseConversation. So persistence landed after that. I found no merge date or commit for it.",
